[User] Replace manual flag parsing with cobra.

[Claude] Added github.com/spf13/cobra dependency. Rewrote main.go to use cobra's command/flag model: two subcommands (convert, distance) with StringVar flags and MarkFlagRequired for required flags. Cobra now handles usage, help text, and error messaging. Note: cobra uses -- prefix for long flags vs the single-dash style in the README examples.

[User] Add support for single-dash flags alongside cobra's double-dash.

[Claude] Added normalizeDashes helper in main.go: walks os.Args before cobra sees them, rewrites any single-dash multi-character flag (e.g. -circuit_model) to double-dash (--circuit_model), leaving single-char flags like -h untouched. Passed normalized args via root.SetArgs. Both -flag and --flag now work.
